# --- FY25 ICFR
add('ICFR conclusion FY25','31-Dec-2025','Based on that evaluation, we concluded that as of December 31, 2025, our internal control over financial reporting was not effective.','NOT EFFECTIVE (2nd year running)','not effective','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.85')
add('Disclosure controls FY25','31-Dec-2025','the company\u2019s principal executive officer and principal financial officer concluded that, as of such date, the company\u2019s disclosure controls and procedures were effective at the reasonable assurance level.','DC&P concluded effective despite two ICFR MWs','effective','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.84')
add('MW link to FY24','FY25 20-F','We reported material weaknesses in our internal control over financial reporting in our 2024 Annual Report on Form 20-F. We have concluded that these material weaknesses reflected the significant growth in our business and the substantial changes in our organization following the complex divestment transaction we completed in 2024. ... we were unable to complete the implementation of all necessary controls during 2025.','Carry-over from FY24','not disclosed','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.85')
add('MW 1 - Fixed assets / PP&E (FY25)','31-Dec-2025','Our controls related to fixed assets were not adequately designed and were not operating effectively. Specifically, we did not fully implement and ensure the effectiveness of the relevant controls and procedures over depreciation start dates, and timely reconciliation around the asset count process. As a result of this deficiency, we were not able to rely on certain data and reports used in the accounting for fixed assets, including server and network equipment, to ensure the completeness and accuracy of such information','OPEN. Covers depreciation start (placed-in-use) dates + asset count reconciliation. First disclosed FY24 20-F (30-Apr-2025)','open','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.85 (also risk factor p.25)')
add('MW 2 - TripleTen ITGC / revenue (FY25)','31-Dec-2025','We did not adequately and timely implement and maintain effective information technology general controls and have not consistently documented the execution of business process controls supporting revenue recognition in respect of our TripleTen business unit (representing approximately 10% of total revenues) commensurate with our financial reporting requirements.','OPEN. Only ITGC MW still open; scoped to TripleTen (~10% of FY25 revenue)','open','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.85')
add('No misstatement (FY25)','FY25','We believe that these control deficiencies did not result in a misstatement to our annual or interim financial statements.','No restatement','none','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.86')
add('Remediated in 2025','FY25','successfully remediated material weaknesses related to revenue recognition in our core business and information technology general controls, as well as a number of other control deficiencies that had been identified as of December 31, 2024.','FY24 MWs (i) business-application ITGC and (ii) core revenue ITGC remediated; fixed-assets MW not','2 of 3 remediated','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.86')
add('Compensating control - depreciation start dates','FY25','We performed compensating control procedures over accuracy of our depreciation start dates for assets acquired in 2025, ensuring the accurate valuation of our fixed assets as of December 31, 2025;','Year-end valuation relied on compensating procedures, not designed controls','not disclosed','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.86')
add('Remediation target date (FY25)','FY25 20-F','We continued to implement a company-wide remediation project, with the support of external consultants ... we expect that this project will improve our information technology systems relating to our fixed assets and revenue recognition reconciliation processes ... We expect to complete this project by the end of 2026.','Target: end-2026 (slipped from Q4-2025 in FY24 20-F)','end of 2026','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.86')
add('Remediation caveat (FY25)','FY25 20-F','We believe we have already made progress and will continue to make progress in our remediation plan during the year ending December 31, 2026, but cannot assure you that we will be able to fully remediate the material weaknesses in 2026.','Risk of 3rd consecutive adverse ICFR opinion for FY26','not disclosed','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.86')
add('Changes in ICFR (FY25)','FY25','In particular, we successfully remediated two material weaknesses that had been identified in the prior period, implemented a robust control framework regarding the revenue recognition process in Nebius AI business and implemented a robust control framework related to our overall IT general controls environment.','','2 MWs remediated','Reported','20F25','Item 15, p.87')
# auditor
add('Auditor ICFR opinion FY25 (adverse)','30-Apr-2026','In our opinion, because of the effect of the material weaknesses described below on the achievement of the objectives of the control criteria, the Company has not maintained effective internal control over financial reporting as of December 31, 2025 ... \u25cf Material weakness in internal controls over property and equipment. \u25cf Material weakness in internal controls over the revenue process for the TripleTen segment.','ADVERSE 404(b) opinion - Reanda Audit & Assurance B.V. (Amsterdam; auditor since 2024). Large accelerated filer; 404(b) box checked','adverse','Reported','20F25','Auditor ICFR report, p.F-5')
add('Auditor FS opinion FY25','30-Apr-2026','these material weaknesses were considered in determining the nature, timing and extent of audit tests applied in our audit of the 2025 consolidated financial statements, and this report does not affect our report dated April 30, 2026 which expressed an unqualified opinion thereon.','Financial statements: UNQUALIFIED','unqualified','Reported','20F25','Auditor ICFR report, p.F-5')
add('CAM - Property and equipment (FY25)','30-Apr-2026','We identified property and equipment as a critical audit matter due to the significant increase in capital expenditure during the year and the judgment involved in determining the timing of placed-in-use dates, the appropriateness of capitalized costs. Auditing these areas required extensive effort and a high degree of auditor judgment.','CAM is on capitalization + placed-in-use dates. The CAM text does NOT mention useful lives or the 4->5 yr change','CAM (PP&E)','Reported','20F25','Auditor FS report, p.F-3/F-4')
add('CAM - PP&E audit procedures','30-Apr-2026','We evaluated management\u2019s determination of placed-in-use dates and tested the timing of depreciation commencement for a sample of assets. We also tested the mathematical accuracy of depreciation expense and evaluated the adequacy of related disclosures.','','not disclosed','Reported','20F25','Auditor FS report, p.F-4')
add('Other CAMs FY25','30-Apr-2026','Revenue Recognition (certain significant customer agreements: service vs lease) ; Investment in ClickHouse (ASC 321 remeasurement, $597.4 upward adjustment)','Three CAMs total: revenue recognition, ClickHouse, PP&E. Useful-life change is not a CAM','3 CAMs','Reported','20F25','Auditor FS report, p.F-2/F-3')
# FY24
add('ICFR conclusion FY24','31-Dec-2024','Based on that evaluation, we concluded that as of December 31, 2024, our internal control over financial reporting was not effective.','FIRST adverse year (FY23 Yandex 20-F concluded ICFR effective)','not effective','Reported','20F24','Item 15, p.76')
add('MW (iii) FY24 - fixed assets','31-Dec-2024','We did not adequately and timely design and maintain effective information systems, policies and procedures for our reconciliation process for fixed assets. Specifically, we did not design, implement and ensure the effectiveness of the relevant operating system controls. In addition, we did not complete our asset validation policy and procedures. This resulted in the ineffectiveness of our ability to ensure the existence, ownership and accuracy of data in connection with our assets, which undermines the assurance of data accuracy and increases the risk of errors or misstatements.','First disclosure of fixed-assets MW (20-F filed 30-Apr-2025); still open at FY25','open','Reported','20F24','Item 15, p.77')
add('MW (i) FY24 - business applications ITGC','31-Dec-2024','We did not adequately and timely design and implement effective controls in business applications across our new information technology infrastructure. Specifically, we did not adequately and timely design, implement and ensure the effectiveness of controls in access management, system monitoring and change management.','Remediated in 2025 (per FY25 20-F)','remediated','Reported','20F24','Item 15, p.77')
add('MW (ii) FY24 - revenue ITGC','31-Dec-2024','Specifically, we did not adequately and timely design, implement and ensure the effectiveness of the operating system controls in connection with our revenue recognition process. This resulted in our inability to consistently establish accurate revenue statements','Remediated for core business in 2025; residual TripleTen MW in FY25','remediated (core)','Reported','20F24','Item 15, p.77')
add('FY24 root cause','FY24','In particular, as we continued to implement a new enterprise resource planning (ERP) system, we did not yet have in place all necessary business processes, systems, personnel, and related internal controls.','New ERP post-divestment','not disclosed','Reported','20F24','Item 15, p.76')
add('FY24 remediation target','FY24 20-F','We conducted a stock count at key asset locations across our businesses to validate the existence, ownership and accuracy of data in connection with our assets as reported for our 2024 fiscal year. ... We expect to complete this project by the fourth quarter of 2025.','Target Q4-2025 -> missed; reset to end-2026 in FY25 20-F','Q4 2025','Reported','20F24','Item 15, p.77')
add('Auditor ICFR opinion FY24 (adverse)','30-Apr-2025','the Company has not maintained effective internal control over financial reporting as of December 31, 2024 ... \u25cf Management also has identified a material weakness in internal controls over fixed assets.','ADVERSE - Reanda Audit & Assurance B.V.','adverse','Reported','20F24','Auditor ICFR report, p.F-4')
add('FY23 baseline','31-Dec-2023','Based on that evaluation, we concluded that as of December 31, 2023, our internal control over financial reporting was effective.','Confirms MWs first disclosed in FY24 20-F','effective','Reported','20F23','Item 15')
add('20-F/A relevance','22-May-2026','is filing this Amendment No. 1 ... solely for the purpose of including Exhibit 97.1. ... does not ... modify or update any of the other disclosures contained therein in any way.','20-F/A is irrelevant to ICFR (adds Ex.97.1 clawback policy only)','n/a','Reported','20FA25','Explanatory Note')
add('Interim reports - remediation update','Q1/Q2 2026','No occurrence of "material weakness", "remediat" or "internal control" in Q1-26 or Q2-26 interim financial statements (Ex.99.2) or interim MD&A/OFR (Ex.99.1).','NO interim remediation update; next status = FY26 20-F (expected ~Apr-2027)','not disclosed','Reported','Q2FS','full-text search of Q1FS, Q1MDA, Q2FS, Q2MDA')
